      "notes": [
        {
          "text": "GTI and NSICT tariffs refer to 'berth hire charges payable to JNPT/JNPA' (idle-time rebate clauses), so JNPA's berth hire is applied at those terminals.",
          "source": {
            "document": "gti-2026",
            "page": 11
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "The JSW JNPT Liquid Terminal tariff says pilotage-cum-towage, port dues, berth hire and anchorage are payable to JNPA as per JNPA's tariff.",
          "source": {
            "document": "jsw-jnpt-liquid-2024",
            "page": 3
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Terminal tariffs have their own dates: NSIGT indexed from 1 April 2026, BMCT from 6 April 2026, NSICT from 1 May 2026. This version uses JNPA's indexed period of 1 May 2026 to 30 April 2027.",
          "source": {
            "document": "nsigt-2026",
            "page": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Ships that also call at Mumbai pay 18% of Mumbai's port dues to JNPA in some cases (section 2.1 note 8); this is not added automatically.",
          "source": {
            "document": "sor-2026-27",
            "page": 3
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "NSIGT and BMCT charge their own berth hire in rupees (also for foreign ships). NSFT's tariff covers container handling only and has no ship charges (no port dues, pilotage or berth hire), so, as at GTI and NSICT, JNPA's all-berths berth hire is applied at NSFT."
        }
      ]
